## Ground rules for the whole build

- **No invented commercial values.** Commission rates, credit pack amounts, package ceilings, file size limits, timeout windows — none of these get hardcoded. Read them from `platform_config` or a JSON config file at runtime. Where a value is not yet confirmed, write `TODO(aya): confirm` in the config with a suggested default clearly marked as a suggestion.
- **Yoco stays isolated.** All Yoco-specific code stays behind a single payment provider module. Switching to PayFast or Paystack later must remain a one-file change. Do not let Yoco types or field names leak into booking or wallet code.
- **Money is integers.** Follow whatever convention already exists in the codebase. If conventions are mixed, tell me before writing anything new.
- **Providers never pay to compete for leads.** Nothing in this build charges a provider to receive, view, or respond to a booking. Commission is charged on completed, paid work only.
- **Legal and policy copy** (cancellation terms, refund terms, dispute wording) gets a `TODO(aya): legal review` placeholder. Do not draft it.
- **Every new table gets RLS.** No table ships with RLS disabled. Every policy gets a test.
- **Migrations are idempotent and additive.** Never drop or rewrite an existing column without flagging it to me first.
- Build in the order below. After each Part, run `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm test`, and report before moving on.

